      en: "Prevalje is a town in the Carinthia region of northern Slovenia, located in the Meža Valley. The name derives from the Slavic word for 'pass'. The settlement was first mentioned in the 13th century. Industrial development began in the 19th century with the establishment of ironworks. The Prevalje Ironworks (Železarna Prevalje) was founded in 1875 and became a major employer. After WWII, the town expanded rapidly. The decline of heavy industry in the 1990s led to economic restructuring. Today, Prevalje is known for its wood and metal processing industries. The Church of Saint Andrew is a Baroque building from 1763. The nearby Peca Mountain was mined for lead and zinc until the late 20th century.",
